  "slug": "depth-compartment-bb23",
  "summary": "Eight preprints show network, gene-set and cell-state conclusions varying with evaluation depth, scoring, composition and replicates, calling for explicit controls.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that transcriptomic and proteomic conclusions depend on analytical choices and biological context. Co-abundance method rankings change with evaluation depth, and colorectal stress granule fibroblast-epithelial contrasts depend on scoring method and depth. Efferocytosis readouts after stroke are bounded by cell composition and time, and replicate-library variation sets the noise floor for cell-state claims in drug-tolerant PC9 cells, where a library-level permutation test is proposed. Compartment specificity recurs in cochlear ageing, which shows weak systemic concordance and a distinct macrophage programme, and in GABAergic channel expression, which reinforces rather than compensates dendritic conductance load. Cell-state conditioning predicts responses to an unseen stimulus but not stimulus-dependent genetic effects. The new emphasis is on stating depth, scoring and replicate structure before interpreting signals, rather than treating readouts as context-free.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
